1
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,265
You mean her truth?

2
00:01:02,345 --> 00:01:04,025
The woman who tore our family apart?!

3
00:01:04,105 --> 00:01:06,225
Neen didn't tear our family apart.

4
00:01:06,305 --> 00:01:08,345
I know a way you can earn money.

5
00:01:14,265 --> 00:01:15,985
The investigators

6
00:01:16,065 --> 00:01:18,985
can't charge her
with solicitation of kidnapping.

7
00:01:19,065 --> 00:01:20,545
Just because she isn't charged

8
00:01:21,505 --> 00:01:22,945
doesn't mean she isn't guilty.

9
00:01:23,025 --> 00:01:24,825
You want me to go to jail that bad?

10
00:01:24,905 --> 00:01:28,345
At least
it will stop you from hurting others,

11
00:01:28,425 --> 00:01:29,585
especially our daughter!

12
00:01:29,665 --> 00:01:31,065
Sooner or later,

13
00:01:31,145 --> 00:01:33,545
she'll get her karma
for what she did to us.

14
00:01:33,625 --> 00:01:34,785
You reap

15
00:01:34,865 --> 00:01:36,985
what you sow.

16
00:01:47,825 --> 00:01:50,025
Nat told me to wait for you in here.

17
00:02:03,705 --> 00:02:04,865
Neen.

18
00:02:09,705 --> 00:02:11,105
Wanna grab some coffee

19
00:02:12,505 --> 00:02:14,345
at our spot?

20
00:02:21,225 --> 00:02:23,145
Do you remember?

21
00:02:24,625 --> 00:02:25,865
This place

22
00:02:26,585 --> 00:02:28,465
is where we first met.

23
00:02:33,625 --> 00:02:34,745
I do.

24
00:02:36,025 --> 00:02:37,225
I never forgot.

25
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:47,745
This is where we started,

26
00:02:49,985 --> 00:02:51,905
so I wanted us to end things here.

27
00:03:07,185 --> 00:03:10,585
SIGNATURE - RUNCHLAPHAT TRIKITTIPHUM
SIGNATURE - PEERACHA PACHARATHAKUL

28
00:03:15,505 --> 00:03:16,865
I signed it already.

29
00:03:31,945 --> 00:03:34,305
Thank you

30
00:03:35,425 --> 00:03:37,545
for all the days we were together.

31
00:03:42,905 --> 00:03:45,865
You always made me really happy.

32
00:03:50,105 --> 00:03:52,745
You made me want to wake up early…

33
00:03:55,025 --> 00:03:57,025
just to see your face.

34
00:04:01,025 --> 00:04:02,985
You made me want to come home…

35
00:04:05,465 --> 00:04:06,905
so I could wait for you.

36
00:04:09,465 --> 00:04:11,865
I would always wonder if you were hungry…

37
00:04:13,625 --> 00:04:14,865
or tired.

38
00:04:21,425 --> 00:04:24,185
You really gave me hope.

39
00:04:34,825 --> 00:04:36,825
I wanted to thank you too.

40
00:04:40,425 --> 00:04:42,985
Thank you for loving me so much

41
00:04:44,985 --> 00:04:46,665
that I felt like…

42
00:04:48,745 --> 00:04:50,265
I matter.

43
00:04:57,105 --> 00:04:58,825
I never imagined

44
00:04:59,705 --> 00:05:02,425
I could mean so much to someone.

45
00:05:20,745 --> 00:05:22,385
Neen.

46
00:05:27,785 --> 00:05:30,025
I want you to know that…

47
00:05:32,305 --> 00:05:34,585
no matter what our relationship is,

48
00:05:38,625 --> 00:05:42,105
you're the best part of my life.

49
00:06:02,225 --> 00:06:03,585
Same here.

50
00:08:21,305 --> 00:08:24,145
TOULOUSE, FRANCE - 2 YEARS LATER

51
00:08:25,385 --> 00:08:27,865
Wow. What is Miss Neen doing this time?

52
00:08:27,945 --> 00:08:28,705
CEO GIRL SPOTTED
GETTING COZY WITH FAMOUS ACTRESS

53
00:08:28,785 --> 00:08:30,585
She's opened a new restaurant.

54
00:08:31,665 --> 00:08:33,144
I thought it was about her dating someone.

55
00:08:35,904 --> 00:08:40,345
She's not a celebrity or a pop idol.
Why would she be in stories like that?

56
00:08:40,425 --> 00:08:42,425
Oh, you're right.

57
00:08:42,505 --> 00:08:46,025
A rich girl like her should be dating
someone in showbiz.

58
00:08:46,105 --> 00:08:49,385
Next time she's in the news,
it'll probably be her wedding.

59
00:08:51,545 --> 00:08:55,585
You know, I never imagined
I'd get to be here either.

60
00:08:56,945 --> 00:08:59,345
That's just how life is.
Nothing is certain.

61
00:08:59,425 --> 00:09:00,945
Who knows?

62
00:09:01,025 --> 00:09:05,185
You might get back together with Neen
and end up remarrying.

63
00:09:07,825 --> 00:09:11,545
If that ever happens, that'd be great.

64
00:09:11,625 --> 00:09:16,345
You won't even consider
starting over with someone new?

65
00:09:19,505 --> 00:09:21,465
Well, I still love her.

66
00:09:24,745 --> 00:09:26,425
I never stopped loving her.

67
00:09:37,265 --> 00:09:39,185
-Were you on a date?
-Huh?

68
00:09:40,505 --> 00:09:43,065
I saw so many pictures
of you and that actress.

69
00:09:44,265 --> 00:09:45,585
What date? We're just friends.

70
00:09:47,425 --> 00:09:49,745
And here I thought
you were dating someone new.

71
00:09:50,985 --> 00:09:53,945
Who would I date?
You don't even date anyone either.

72
00:09:54,545 --> 00:09:56,905
I don't date because I'm busy.

73
00:09:56,985 --> 00:09:59,665
But you know why you're not dating?

74
00:10:01,385 --> 00:10:04,745
Stop saying bad things about Runch,
or I'll get mad at you.

75
00:10:05,345 --> 00:10:07,425
You're always defending
your wife, aren't you?

76
00:10:08,025 --> 00:10:10,225
Oh. I mean, your ex-wife.

77
00:10:11,625 --> 00:10:15,385
So, where did you see the photos?

78
00:10:15,465 --> 00:10:19,425
Well, everyone's sharing them online.
She's a famous actress too, right?

79
00:10:20,105 --> 00:10:21,265
It's a big deal right now.

80
00:10:21,345 --> 00:10:23,905
Are you sure you're not interested?

81
00:10:25,665 --> 00:10:27,025
It's really nothing, right?

82
00:10:29,105 --> 00:10:33,425
Well, she was hitting on me.
I already rejected her, though.

83
00:10:33,505 --> 00:10:37,785
You would really reject a lead actress?

84
00:10:37,865 --> 00:10:40,145
Stop taking a dig at Runch, will you?

85
00:10:40,225 --> 00:10:42,585
Okay. I guess
you're not over your darling.

86
00:10:42,665 --> 00:10:43,665
Nai!

87
00:10:44,305 --> 00:10:46,265
I bet your darling
has seen the news by now

88
00:10:46,345 --> 00:10:51,465
that her ex-wife was seen
getting cozy with a lead actress.

89
00:10:51,545 --> 00:10:53,665
She probably doesn't
care about me anymore.

90
00:10:54,465 --> 00:10:55,905
Who knows?

91
00:10:57,465 --> 00:10:58,465
What's gotten into you?

92
00:10:58,545 --> 00:11:00,825
You were the one
who wanted me to divorce her so badly.

93
00:11:02,585 --> 00:11:06,305
I guess it's because I see now
that you cannot love anyone else,

94
00:11:06,385 --> 00:11:08,465
if it's not that beautiful woman.

95
00:11:09,185 --> 00:11:12,305
Look, I don't have an issue
with being alone,

96
00:11:12,385 --> 00:11:14,625
nor am I incapable
of loving someone new. Got it?

97
00:11:14,705 --> 00:11:16,465
Are you sure you don't have an issue?

98
00:11:16,545 --> 00:11:20,065
You were still crying at a wedding
thinking of Runch, so I'm not too sure.

99
00:11:21,105 --> 00:11:23,665
That Plengpin just
cannot keep a secret, can she?

100
00:11:24,585 --> 00:11:27,385
Crying because you miss your ex-wife

101
00:11:28,465 --> 00:11:31,105
-is perfectly normal.
-Do you have an ex-wife too?

102
00:11:31,185 --> 00:11:34,265
No. And I don't want to either.

103
00:11:34,345 --> 00:11:36,705
But if you don't want her
to be just an ex-wife,

104
00:11:37,945 --> 00:11:41,345
you know what to do, right?
Or do I need to tell you?

105
00:11:42,385 --> 00:11:46,865
No need. I'm not doing anything.
When it's over, it's over. For good.

106
00:11:46,945 --> 00:11:49,345
We split up for good. It's over.

107
00:11:50,865 --> 00:11:53,505
-I'll wait and see.
-Fine. You'll see.

108
00:12:00,305 --> 00:12:04,665
1 MONTH LATER

109
00:12:11,265 --> 00:12:12,425
Neen!

110
00:12:12,505 --> 00:12:15,265
-Oh. Hi, Dad.
-Hi.

111
00:12:15,345 --> 00:12:17,225
It's been a while.

112
00:12:17,305 --> 00:12:19,825
Yes. How have you been?

113
00:12:19,905 --> 00:12:22,345
I've been alright.
It's been a bit of a struggle.

114
00:12:22,425 --> 00:12:24,265
-Mostly okay.
-I see.

115
00:12:24,345 --> 00:12:27,265
What are you up to around here today?

116
00:12:28,865 --> 00:12:30,385
I'm here to meet…

117
00:12:30,465 --> 00:12:34,145
Oh. I'll get out of your hair, then.
If you'll excuse me.

118
00:12:34,225 --> 00:12:35,785
-See you later.
-Alright.

119
00:12:52,345 --> 00:12:54,345
-Hi, Dad.
-Hi, honey.

120
00:12:54,425 --> 00:12:56,825
-When did you get here?
-About ten minutes ago.

121
00:12:56,905 --> 00:12:59,185
I already ordered some food.
Help yourself.

122
00:12:59,785 --> 00:13:02,665
Wow. Thank you.

123
00:13:02,745 --> 00:13:06,105
I just want Thai food today.
I really missed it.

124
00:13:06,185 --> 00:13:07,985
Anything will do.

125
00:13:15,945 --> 00:13:18,025
-Runch.
-Yes?

126
00:13:18,105 --> 00:13:20,145
I ran into Neen earlier.

127
00:13:20,225 --> 00:13:22,465
She was still calling me "Dad."

128
00:13:30,665 --> 00:13:33,625
How has Mom been doing?

129
00:13:34,385 --> 00:13:36,785
She's a lot calmer now.

130
00:13:36,865 --> 00:13:40,105
She's probably realized
there's nothing she can do.

131
00:13:40,985 --> 00:13:45,305
They scammed me! Those low-life scammers!

132
00:13:45,385 --> 00:13:48,705
My life savings
and my retirement pay… All gone!

133
00:13:48,785 --> 00:13:51,105
Why throw a fit?
That won't earn your money back.

134
00:13:51,185 --> 00:13:52,585
What do you want me to do, then?!

135
00:13:56,145 --> 00:13:59,105
Who would've known that bank teller
would turn out to be a scammer?

136
00:13:59,185 --> 00:14:01,905
What bank teller would call you
asking you to transfer money?

137
00:14:03,985 --> 00:14:08,185
I just wanted my money to grow.
I didn't do anything wrong.

138
00:14:08,265 --> 00:14:09,265
Really?

139
00:14:09,345 --> 00:14:11,865
There's news about people
getting scammed everywhere.

140
00:14:11,945 --> 00:14:13,225
You really haven't seen it?

141
00:14:13,305 --> 00:14:14,905
Are you blaming me?

142
00:14:14,985 --> 00:14:17,305
I'm not. I'm just telling the truth.

143
00:14:17,385 --> 00:14:19,865
And you know what we have to do?
We have to sell the house.

144
00:14:19,945 --> 00:14:22,945
Are you crazy? This is our house!

145
00:14:23,745 --> 00:14:25,025
If anything,

146
00:14:25,105 --> 00:14:26,985
we should ask Runch for help.

147
00:14:27,065 --> 00:14:29,785
Did you already forget
what you did to her?

148
00:14:29,865 --> 00:14:31,785
There's no way she'll help us.

149
00:14:31,865 --> 00:14:35,385
You caused all these problems alone,
and you want her to take responsibility?

150
00:14:46,905 --> 00:14:48,785
How do I live?

151
00:14:50,785 --> 00:14:52,985
Like a normal person,

152
00:14:53,065 --> 00:14:54,905
something you never wanted to be.

153
00:14:56,545 --> 00:14:58,745
Or if there's nowhere left to turn to,

154
00:14:58,825 --> 00:15:00,185
come join me at the temple.

155
00:15:00,745 --> 00:15:03,225
No, no!

156
00:15:07,385 --> 00:15:10,065
How am I supposed to live now?!

157
00:15:21,305 --> 00:15:23,185
It's probably for the best.

158
00:15:24,665 --> 00:15:27,425
Otherwise, she'd still
be causing trouble non-stop.

159
00:15:28,065 --> 00:15:29,425
Yeah.

160
00:15:30,865 --> 00:15:33,665
How long will you
be staying here this time?

161
00:15:33,745 --> 00:15:36,105
About a month.

162
00:15:36,185 --> 00:15:40,585
Then after that, I'll be in France
for a while until I graduate.

163
00:15:42,265 --> 00:15:45,185
Will you go see Neen before then?

164
00:16:10,865 --> 00:16:12,345
One americano, please.

165
00:16:13,065 --> 00:16:14,465
Oh! Hello, beautiful.

166
00:16:14,545 --> 00:16:15,905
Where have you been?

167
00:16:15,985 --> 00:16:17,625
Long time no see.

168
00:16:18,425 --> 00:16:20,265
Americano, as always, right?

169
00:16:20,345 --> 00:16:21,385
Yes, please.

170
00:16:22,905 --> 00:16:26,905
Oh. I thought you were here alone.
Your girlfriend came too?

171
00:16:46,825 --> 00:16:48,425
I missed you.

172
00:16:49,545 --> 00:16:51,585
You're saying that right away, huh?

173
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:53,545
Yes.

174
00:16:57,665 --> 00:17:00,905
At lunch, Dad told me he ran into you.

175
00:17:02,145 --> 00:17:05,025
Well? Were you hoping to run into me too?

176
00:17:05,105 --> 00:17:05,944
Yes.

177
00:17:06,545 --> 00:17:07,825
I was.

178
00:17:09,464 --> 00:17:11,625
You are way too honest, Runchlaphat.

179
00:17:22,464 --> 00:17:23,625
Going already?

180
00:17:25,985 --> 00:17:27,025
Yeah.

181
00:17:27,105 --> 00:17:28,825
Can I come with you?

182
00:17:29,985 --> 00:17:31,665
You mean you need a ride?

183
00:17:31,745 --> 00:17:32,785
I mean,

184
00:17:33,505 --> 00:17:34,745
I want to come with you.

185
00:17:35,705 --> 00:17:37,145
To your place.

186
00:17:42,185 --> 00:17:43,625
To stay the night with me?

187
00:17:46,145 --> 00:17:47,705
Can I?

188
00:17:52,105 --> 00:17:54,865
Look, Gorgeous.

189
00:17:57,465 --> 00:17:58,985
Yes?

190
00:18:01,225 --> 00:18:05,625
If we're going to do this,
we both need to be single.

191
00:18:06,585 --> 00:18:08,385
Well, I am.

192
00:18:09,585 --> 00:18:10,985
I always have been.

193
00:18:13,225 --> 00:18:14,705
Don't tell me…

194
00:18:16,425 --> 00:18:17,785
you're dating someone?

195
00:18:17,865 --> 00:18:19,265
I'm also single.

196
00:18:26,865 --> 00:18:28,345
But are you sure you want to come?

197
00:18:45,905 --> 00:18:49,425
My parents and Nai are in the US.
No one's home.

198
00:18:49,505 --> 00:18:51,625
You're home alone?

199
00:18:53,945 --> 00:18:55,185
Yes.

200
00:18:59,225 --> 00:19:01,065
Do you need anything besides water?

201
00:19:01,145 --> 00:19:02,505
No, thanks.

202
00:19:04,185 --> 00:19:07,665
Then let's shower.
I'll find you a pair of pajamas.

203
00:19:10,065 --> 00:19:12,145
Which room am I staying in?

204
00:19:12,945 --> 00:19:14,385
In another room.

205
00:19:21,145 --> 00:19:22,785
Or did you want to be in my room?

206
00:19:25,345 --> 00:19:26,705
Can I?

207
00:19:29,305 --> 00:19:32,345
Of course not. Don't be silly.

208
00:19:37,985 --> 00:19:40,025
Then any room will do.

209
00:19:42,505 --> 00:19:45,185
Of course. Let's go.

210
00:19:46,865 --> 00:19:48,185
Hold on.

211
00:19:51,465 --> 00:19:53,105
Can we sit down and talk first?

212
00:20:04,905 --> 00:20:07,545
How have you been in the past two years?

213
00:20:09,945 --> 00:20:13,985
I've been alright.
I just work and go home every day.

214
00:20:14,065 --> 00:20:16,385
In a loop. Nothing significant.

215
00:20:17,065 --> 00:20:18,305
What about you?

216
00:20:20,065 --> 00:20:24,625
I went to study in France
not long after we got divorced.

217
00:20:27,105 --> 00:20:28,105
Over there,

218
00:20:28,185 --> 00:20:30,625
Natee helped me in so many ways.

219
00:20:33,545 --> 00:20:35,385
The classes are super hard.

220
00:20:36,025 --> 00:20:39,385
Sometimes, I wondered
why I even went in the first place.

221
00:20:40,625 --> 00:20:42,505
When do you graduate?

222
00:20:43,265 --> 00:20:45,665
I'm trying to graduate this year.

223
00:20:49,385 --> 00:20:50,585
So…

224
00:20:51,265 --> 00:20:53,025
will you be back?

225
00:20:56,145 --> 00:20:57,585
Of course.

226
00:21:10,985 --> 00:21:12,865
Ever since the incident,

227
00:21:14,505 --> 00:21:16,825
I never contacted my mother again.

228
00:21:20,545 --> 00:21:23,065
I cut her off financially too.

229
00:21:27,145 --> 00:21:29,665
She has no idea
where I am or what I'm doing.

230
00:21:40,385 --> 00:21:42,465
Is it tough over there in France?

231
00:21:49,265 --> 00:21:50,465
Of course.

232
00:21:54,665 --> 00:21:56,545
It was tough because I missed you.

233
00:21:59,265 --> 00:22:01,425
You'd better watch what you say.

234
00:22:01,505 --> 00:22:03,385
We already got divorced, Runch.

235
00:22:13,785 --> 00:22:15,425
I really did miss you, though.

236
00:22:21,105 --> 00:22:22,545
Yes.

237
00:22:23,705 --> 00:22:25,545
I really missed you too.

238
00:22:37,345 --> 00:22:38,705
Can I kiss you?

239
00:22:41,505 --> 00:22:42,945
You can do way more than that.

240
00:23:56,305 --> 00:23:58,585
Why are you up so early, Neen?

241
00:24:00,985 --> 00:24:04,545
I… I need to go to work.

242
00:24:07,625 --> 00:24:10,025
Call in sick and stay with me.

243
00:24:11,345 --> 00:24:15,145
This time, I'll be in France for a while.

244
00:24:16,745 --> 00:24:21,025
Stay with me. Please? Please?

245
00:24:21,105 --> 00:24:24,425
Runch… Don't do that.

246
00:24:27,065 --> 00:24:28,305
Why not?

247
00:24:29,385 --> 00:24:30,945
Am I making you blush?

248
00:24:31,625 --> 00:24:33,465
How could I not?

249
00:24:34,105 --> 00:24:35,665
It's been two whole years.

250
00:24:35,745 --> 00:24:39,065
We just saw each other again
and ended up in bed right away.

251
00:24:40,385 --> 00:24:42,305
This can't be right, Runch.

252
00:24:44,065 --> 00:24:45,505
You were drunk. That's why.

253
00:24:48,145 --> 00:24:50,305
I wasn't.

254
00:24:50,385 --> 00:24:52,545
I was fully in control.

255
00:24:53,545 --> 00:24:54,865
I did it all on purpose.

256
00:24:59,385 --> 00:25:01,225
Please stay.

257
00:25:01,985 --> 00:25:05,505
I missed you so bad,
and I don't want to waste any time.

258
00:25:05,585 --> 00:25:08,465
Please, please, please?

259
00:25:08,545 --> 00:25:10,625
Quite smooth, aren't you?

260
00:25:13,025 --> 00:25:15,625
Only with you.

261
00:25:15,705 --> 00:25:17,305
So don't worry.

262
00:25:47,145 --> 00:25:49,865
I was so happy last night.

263
00:25:52,065 --> 00:25:54,505
Because you got to sleep with a girl?

264
00:25:56,305 --> 00:25:58,945
Because I got to sleep with you.

265
00:26:02,265 --> 00:26:04,785
I didn't tell you last night

266
00:26:06,105 --> 00:26:07,305
that I…

267
00:26:08,105 --> 00:26:09,185
still love you.

268
00:26:11,665 --> 00:26:13,105
I never stopped loving you.

269
00:26:14,185 --> 00:26:16,145
I've always loved you just the same.

270
00:26:19,585 --> 00:26:21,305
You're being all sweet. What do you want?

271
00:26:25,985 --> 00:26:28,345
If I told you

272
00:26:30,505 --> 00:26:32,625
I want you as my wife,

273
00:26:36,265 --> 00:26:37,745
would that be possible?

274
00:27:00,625 --> 00:27:04,745
I'm so glad
Dad hasn't sold this house yet,

275
00:27:05,825 --> 00:27:08,305
so we get to see each other every day.

276
00:27:11,345 --> 00:27:12,385
Yeah.

277
00:27:12,905 --> 00:27:17,825
But my parents are starting to wonder
why I'm staying here every night.

278
00:27:18,585 --> 00:27:20,945
So I told them,

279
00:27:21,025 --> 00:27:24,985
"Work's been busy,
and this house is closer to work."

280
00:27:25,065 --> 00:27:28,185
Well done. That's my good girl.

281
00:27:37,105 --> 00:27:38,305
Neen.

282
00:27:39,105 --> 00:27:40,505
Yes?

283
00:27:43,545 --> 00:27:44,945
Will you marry me?

284
00:27:51,945 --> 00:27:53,785
Isn't it too soon?

285
00:27:55,705 --> 00:27:57,905
I will make sure

286
00:27:59,185 --> 00:28:01,025
things are different this time

287
00:28:02,625 --> 00:28:03,985
when we get married again.

288
00:28:05,625 --> 00:28:07,785
I promise it won't be the same.

289
00:28:12,705 --> 00:28:14,345
But if you don't want that…

290
00:28:17,265 --> 00:28:19,345
will you be my girlfriend first?

291
00:28:21,665 --> 00:28:23,305
Will it be weird?

292
00:28:24,425 --> 00:28:26,225
To date again

293
00:28:26,305 --> 00:28:28,185
all of a sudden?

294
00:28:30,905 --> 00:28:32,465
It won't be.

295
00:28:35,025 --> 00:28:38,785
You'll be studying abroad anyway,
so what's the hurry?

296
00:28:39,585 --> 00:28:41,585
I will graduate as soon as I can

297
00:28:42,185 --> 00:28:43,545
so I can come back.

298
00:28:46,265 --> 00:28:48,385
If I say yes now,

299
00:28:48,465 --> 00:28:51,705
we'll be in
a long-distance relationship, right?

300
00:28:53,025 --> 00:28:54,985
-Then sure.
-What?

301
00:28:55,065 --> 00:28:56,705
I'm saying yes.

302
00:28:58,745 --> 00:29:01,265
Just don't date anyone while you're there.

303
00:29:01,345 --> 00:29:02,545
I won't.

304
00:29:03,785 --> 00:29:06,985
Are you happy now that
I'm your girlfriend again?

305
00:29:07,945 --> 00:29:09,505
Of course I am.

306
00:29:10,425 --> 00:29:12,625
I'm over the moon.

307
00:29:12,705 --> 00:29:14,985
I used to be your wife, you know.

308
00:29:15,905 --> 00:29:18,505
Well, if we marry again,

309
00:29:19,505 --> 00:29:22,185
I'll be so happy I'll cry.

310
00:29:49,585 --> 00:29:53,785
What's so great about France?
You've been flying there every month.

311
00:29:53,865 --> 00:29:55,305
Answer me.

312
00:29:55,385 --> 00:29:58,625
Well, maybe I just want to travel.

313
00:29:58,705 --> 00:30:01,305
Why would you travel every month?

314
00:30:01,905 --> 00:30:04,825
Don't tell me you found a new girlfriend.

315
00:30:04,905 --> 00:30:07,305
-A French woman? How did you two meet?
-No.

316
00:30:07,385 --> 00:30:08,905
Calm down.

317
00:30:08,985 --> 00:30:10,625
I don't have a new girlfriend.

318
00:30:10,705 --> 00:30:11,785
Well?

319
00:30:11,865 --> 00:30:13,065
It's my ex.

320
00:30:14,385 --> 00:30:16,425
-Oh my god!
-My god! Since when?

321
00:30:16,505 --> 00:30:17,465
But how?

322
00:30:17,545 --> 00:30:18,505
What happened?

323
00:30:18,585 --> 00:30:22,985
We just so happened
to run into each other, and…

324
00:30:23,065 --> 00:30:26,145
And? And you two ended up in bed, I bet.

325
00:30:27,825 --> 00:30:29,745
Alright, Ms. Know-It-All.

326
00:30:29,825 --> 00:30:30,905
Hold on.

327
00:30:30,985 --> 00:30:33,105
Your new girlfriend is your ex-wife?

328
00:30:35,785 --> 00:30:38,385
Wow. You must really like her.

329
00:30:38,465 --> 00:30:39,705
-Stop teasing me.
-I see a smile.

330
00:30:39,785 --> 00:30:41,745
Does it still feel the same?

331
00:30:41,825 --> 00:30:44,985
Like when you were hitting on her,
and when you started dating?

332
00:30:49,705 --> 00:30:53,185
Well, it feels the same sometimes.

333
00:30:53,945 --> 00:30:55,465
She's changed a little.

334
00:30:55,545 --> 00:30:57,705
But in a good way.

335
00:30:58,305 --> 00:31:00,665
And will you get married again?

336
00:31:01,425 --> 00:31:02,465
I don't know.

337
00:31:03,105 --> 00:31:07,505
I've gotten married
and registered my marriage before.

338
00:31:07,585 --> 00:31:12,305
And none of that could guarantee
that Runch and I would last.

339
00:31:12,385 --> 00:31:13,585
Yeah.

340
00:31:14,785 --> 00:31:16,905
Anyway, we'll see about that.

341
00:31:17,425 --> 00:31:18,345
I understand.

342
00:31:18,425 --> 00:31:20,945
Still, we're happy to hear

343
00:31:21,025 --> 00:31:22,505
you gave her a second chance,

344
00:31:23,105 --> 00:31:24,705
and yourself too.

345
00:31:24,785 --> 00:31:26,585
It'll definitely be better this time.

346
00:31:28,505 --> 00:31:29,665
Well, I hope so.

347
00:31:41,385 --> 00:31:42,465
Neen!

348
00:31:49,625 --> 00:31:50,545
Come here.

349
00:31:55,545 --> 00:31:58,305
Wait, wait. Calm down, Neen.

350
00:31:58,385 --> 00:32:01,545
No way. I missed you. I missed you so bad.

351
00:32:01,625 --> 00:32:05,305
I kept wishing there was a portal
leading straight to your room.

352
00:32:05,385 --> 00:32:07,625
I'm tired of flying for several hours.

353
00:32:08,465 --> 00:32:10,545
Relax, Neen.

354
00:32:11,185 --> 00:32:13,545
I was hoping to take you out for a walk.

355
00:32:13,625 --> 00:32:15,185
There's a new café in town.

356
00:32:15,265 --> 00:32:18,345
It just opened
after you flew back last month.

357
00:32:20,465 --> 00:32:21,705
Neen, honey…

358
00:32:21,785 --> 00:32:22,785
Yes?

359
00:32:23,305 --> 00:32:25,865
How about we go out after an hour?

360
00:32:26,665 --> 00:32:28,385
You sure that's enough?

361
00:32:28,465 --> 00:32:30,825
I guess more than an hour is fine.

362
00:32:40,905 --> 00:32:43,265
I missed you so much.

363
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:08,025
Let me see that.

364
00:33:08,105 --> 00:33:11,825
You know, I really love oranges.
Let me see that one too.

365
00:33:11,905 --> 00:33:14,065
Orange cheeks!

366
00:33:15,905 --> 00:33:18,465
Actually, let's not buy those yet.

367
00:33:18,545 --> 00:33:20,825
Yeah, they're heavy. Let's buy them later.

368
00:33:30,225 --> 00:33:31,305
I'll buy…

369
00:33:31,825 --> 00:33:33,705
this one.

370
00:33:34,745 --> 00:33:36,985
-How much is this?
-Five euros.

371
00:33:38,505 --> 00:33:39,425
Thank you.

372
00:33:44,225 --> 00:33:45,625
This is for you.

373
00:33:50,065 --> 00:33:52,745
-Thank you, baby.
-For you.

374
00:34:28,025 --> 00:34:29,905
-Let me have a bite.
-Here.

375
00:34:32,865 --> 00:34:33,744
All yours.

376
00:34:44,824 --> 00:34:50,585
3 YEARS LATER

377
00:34:53,425 --> 00:34:55,945
Hello, Professor Runchlaphat.

378
00:34:56,025 --> 00:34:58,545
What time does your class finish today?

379
00:34:58,625 --> 00:35:01,505
At five. Why?

380
00:35:01,585 --> 00:35:04,225
Nothing. I was just wondering.

381
00:35:04,305 --> 00:35:07,945
You should hurry home, though.
I have a surprise for you.

382
00:35:25,105 --> 00:35:26,665
Let's see here.

383
00:35:29,305 --> 00:35:31,785
This is the surprise
you were talking about?

384
00:35:32,785 --> 00:35:34,705
-Where did you buy them?
-Hey!

385
00:35:35,425 --> 00:35:38,345
That's so insulting.
I made them all myself.

386
00:35:38,425 --> 00:35:41,185
-Really?
-Yeah. Try it if you don't believe me.

387
00:35:41,265 --> 00:35:43,385
I assure you,
this time you won't spit it out.

388
00:36:03,185 --> 00:36:04,545
It really is great!

389
00:36:07,025 --> 00:36:09,225
Looks like those cooking lessons
really paid off.

390
00:36:10,465 --> 00:36:14,665
Tell me. Would you want me

391
00:36:14,745 --> 00:36:18,585
to cook every meal for you from now on?

392
00:36:21,105 --> 00:36:23,585
Of course. That would be amazing.

393
00:36:24,545 --> 00:36:27,225
What about desserts?

394
00:36:28,585 --> 00:36:30,345
You know how to make them?

395
00:36:33,265 --> 00:36:35,505
I wouldn't need to take lessons for that.

396
00:36:55,025 --> 00:36:56,425
See?

397
00:36:57,065 --> 00:36:58,705
I'm the best dessert.

398
00:37:07,065 --> 00:37:09,185
Take off your glasses before you kiss me.

399
00:37:10,185 --> 00:37:11,425
They're in the way.

400
00:37:35,065 --> 00:37:38,665
We want to ask you something personal
this time. Is that okay, Ms. Neen?

401
00:37:39,505 --> 00:37:40,465
Sure.

402
00:37:40,545 --> 00:37:43,185
As we all know, you've gotten married
and divorced before.

403
00:37:43,265 --> 00:37:45,225
It had many people wondering

404
00:37:45,305 --> 00:37:48,065
how someone like you
could have a rocky relationship?

405
00:37:51,465 --> 00:37:55,825
Honestly, I think anyone
can go through a rough patch.

406
00:37:57,345 --> 00:38:01,185
Especially when it comes to
relationships or marriages, which are

407
00:38:01,265 --> 00:38:02,465
very sensitive topics.

408
00:38:02,545 --> 00:38:06,225
They're also beyond our control,
and just complicated in general.

409
00:38:07,865 --> 00:38:10,385
But things are going great now, right?

410
00:38:10,465 --> 00:38:13,145
Of course. My wife is so sweet.

411
00:38:13,225 --> 00:38:16,905
And I believe I am a sweet wife too.

412
00:38:16,985 --> 00:38:20,185
You seem so happy
when you talk about your wife.

413
00:38:20,785 --> 00:38:24,545
Of course. I'm happy
whenever I see her face.

414
00:38:24,625 --> 00:38:28,025
And I'm happy
whenever I speak of her or think of her.

415
00:38:38,065 --> 00:38:39,505
You know,

416
00:38:40,825 --> 00:38:42,705
I used to think

417
00:38:43,425 --> 00:38:46,545
marriage was about
getting people to accept us.

418
00:38:48,785 --> 00:38:51,185
But once we lost everything,

419
00:38:51,265 --> 00:38:55,185
only then I realized,
it has nothing to do with anyone.

420
00:39:01,265 --> 00:39:02,785
This time,

421
00:39:03,385 --> 00:39:05,905
I don't want to prove anything to anyone.

422
00:39:06,865 --> 00:39:08,425
I don't want to win against anyone

423
00:39:09,465 --> 00:39:11,625
or explain anything.

424
00:39:12,225 --> 00:39:14,305
I just want to ask you…

425
00:39:16,225 --> 00:39:20,265
Since you're a woman
who's learned quite a lot about love,

426
00:39:24,665 --> 00:39:27,225
will you marry me again?

427
00:40:00,985 --> 00:40:02,425
Well? Neen?

428
00:40:06,265 --> 00:40:09,545
Will you marry me again?

429
00:40:34,465 --> 00:40:35,385
Yes.

430
00:40:38,425 --> 00:40:40,105
But this time,

431
00:40:41,065 --> 00:40:43,345
it's not to prove anything to anyone.

432
00:40:46,865 --> 00:40:47,985
I'm doing it

433
00:40:49,625 --> 00:40:52,065
because my heart chooses you.

434
00:41:00,625 --> 00:41:02,225
I promise

435
00:41:03,785 --> 00:41:05,145
to love you

436
00:41:06,545 --> 00:41:08,505
and care about your feelings.

437
00:41:10,305 --> 00:41:11,545
I will be faithful.

438
00:41:14,825 --> 00:41:18,665
And I promise to stay right by your side

439
00:41:19,505 --> 00:41:21,105
through thick

440
00:41:22,065 --> 00:41:23,545
and thin.

441
00:41:26,065 --> 00:41:27,665
I love you, Neen.

442
00:41:28,945 --> 00:41:30,825
You're the only one I love.

443
00:41:31,905 --> 00:41:34,185
Forever.

444
00:41:37,625 --> 00:41:39,385
I love you too.

445
00:41:40,985 --> 00:41:42,505
You're the only one I love.

446
00:41:43,145 --> 00:41:44,785
Forever.

447
00:43:11,385 --> 00:43:15,105
My baby, don't run!

448
00:43:20,705 --> 00:43:25,145
Calm down, baby.
Mommy still hasn't prepared your food.

449
00:43:26,185 --> 00:43:28,185
How did you just refer to yourself?

450
00:43:28,265 --> 00:43:29,985
I said "Mommy."

451
00:43:30,065 --> 00:43:32,945
So what should our baby call me?

452
00:43:33,705 --> 00:43:35,385
You're her other mommy.

453
00:43:42,385 --> 00:43:43,505
Are you hungry yet?

454
00:43:44,745 --> 00:43:46,665
Are you hungry yet?

455
00:43:50,825 --> 00:43:52,625
Now

456
00:43:52,705 --> 00:43:55,025
it really feels like we're starting over.

457
00:43:57,105 --> 00:43:59,985
It's not exactly starting over.

458
00:44:00,065 --> 00:44:03,065
It's more like starting our relationship

459
00:44:03,145 --> 00:44:05,345
in the way we always wanted.

460
00:44:07,505 --> 00:44:10,865
So, it's us three taking care
of each other, right?

461
00:44:12,825 --> 00:44:16,625
Yes. This is our family.

462
00:45:34,505 --> 00:45:39,145
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya

